    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1955-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Using common logarithms, \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\log x&=5\\log3-2\\\\ &=\\log(3^5)-\\log100\\\\ &=\\log\\left(\\frac{243}{100}\\right). \\end{aligned} \\] Therefore \\(x=2.43.\\)\n\nThe correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Move \\(5\\log3\\) to the other side",
        "Use \\(-2=\\log10^{-2}\\) and combine logarithms"
      ],
